<title>DENMARK: Borealis award Abu Dhabi project contract.</title>
<headline>Borealis award Abu Dhabi project contract.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polyolefins maker Borealis A/S said in a statement on Tuesday it agreed with Abu Dhabi National Oil Company (ADNOC) to award a project management consultancy services contract for their joint venture in the Gulf Emirate to Fluor Middle East Limited.</p>
<p>It said Fluor, a subsidiary of Fluor Daniel Inc., would provide design, engineering, procurement and construction services for new petrochemical facilities in Ruwais.</p>
<p>It said the facilities included one ethylene unit, two polyethylene units and utilities at the site in the United Arab Emirates, due for start up in late 2000.</p>
<p>Borealis, 50/50 owned by Finnish energy group Neste Oy and Norwegian Statoil, is the largest producer in Europe of polyolefin plastics and the fifth largest in the world.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
